<title>PERU: Argentina's Pluspetrol to invest $50 mln in Peru.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Pluspetrol to invest $50 mln in Peru.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Pluspetrol Energy SA on Monday said it would invest about $50 million this year on its two energy exploration and exploitation contracts in the northern jungle of Peru.</p>
<p>The company also plans to invest $45 million next year, Alberto Moon's Pluspetrol's general manager in Peru, said in an interview.</p>
<p>In this year's investment program Pluspetrol will spend between $37 million and $40 million in its Block 8 area and $11 million in the Lancones block, Moons said.</p>
<p>He gave no details of next year's spending plans.</p>
<p>((-- Guillermo Pena, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
